    "description": "An early relative of elephants from the late Eocene and early Oligocene swamp forests of Egypt, about 2.5 m long and 1.3 m tall at the shoulder. It probably had a short trunk, with a pair of short tusks in the upper jaw and flat, shovel-like lower teeth for cutting and scooping up water plants. It shows how the trunk and tusks of elephants began."
