    "description": "The largest multituberculate, a beaver-sized mammal about 80 cm long from the early Paleocene of New Mexico, living just a few hundred thousand years after the dinosaurs died out. Multituberculates were an old, rodent-like lineage unrelated to true rodents; Taeniolabis had a deep skull, big gnawing front teeth and broad grinding cheek teeth for tough plants. The group had thrived for over 100 million years before rodents replaced it."
